Tom Cat wrote:
> So WTF happened?

You angered the priest's deity. The Nethack Gods are vengeful and not
averse to chucking out lightning bolts and the like to dispense with
upstart mortals who displease them. With reflection, however, lightning
ceases to be a threat. The deity won't ecessarily give up though.

>The only time I've ever been able to kill the priest
> and convert the alter is when I had a wand of death.  I know from past
> experience that you've got to kill the priest before converting the
> alter, otherwise they get a couple of free hits and kill you.

Converting an altar doesn't paralyse you, so the priest shouldn't get
any free hits- certainly not more than one anyway, unless you are
burdened or the priest is fast or something- so you can convert the
altar first. That spares you the wrath of the other God (although I
believe it's still possible to get some minions thrown in, but someone
may correct me on this. You won't get lightning anyway.)
However it will put you in immediate range of the priest when he
becomes angry. Unless you're really sure you can take him toe to toe,
teleport out and then deal with him at range.



